//!
//! # Sched
//!
//! Kernel threads on one processor: the thread table, the run queue and the
//! switch between threads, cooperative and driven by the timer.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name               | File            | Purpose                                                             |
//! |--------------------|-----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Sched::Scheduler` | `scheduler.ign` | `spawn`, `yield`, `sleep`, `exitCurrent`, preemption, the run queue |
//! | `Sched::Thread`    | `thread.ign`    | the thread table, thread states and the thread stacks               |
//!
//! Sleeping and waking are part of `Sched::Scheduler`: `sleep` and the wake-up
//! scan call `switchToNext`, and `switchToNext` calls the wake-up scan, so
//! they cannot live in separate files without an import cycle.
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports | Why                                                            |
//! |---------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Arch`  | context switch, TSS and `SYSCALL` kernel stack, interrupt flag |
//! | `Mm`    | stack frames, stack mappings, the page tables a thread runs in |
//! | `Time`  | the tick counter that sleeping threads wait for                |
//!
//! `Proc` and `Syscall` import `Sched`, and `Trap` calls
//! `Sched::Scheduler::onTick` from the timer interrupt.

import _ from "./scheduler";
import _ from "./thread";

/// Aggregate namespace of the scheduler. The files above contribute
/// `Sched::Scheduler` and `Sched::Thread`.
export namespace Sched {}
